1
00:00:00,066 --> 00:00:01,434
(This drama complied with production
guidelines for filming child actors,)

2
00:00:01,534 --> 00:00:03,069
(and some scenes used
generative AI technology.)

3
00:00:03,403 --> 00:00:03,821
(Episode 29)

4
00:00:03,904 --> 00:00:04,971
Mom!

5
00:00:05,338 --> 00:00:07,707
What on earth have you done?

6
00:00:07,974 --> 00:00:10,093
A mortgage on the house...

7
00:00:10,176 --> 00:00:12,529
It's supposed to need consent
from everyone living here,

8
00:00:12,612 --> 00:00:14,481
Doesn't the bank even check that?

9
00:00:15,715 --> 00:00:17,951
I signed it for you.

10
00:00:21,554 --> 00:00:23,823
- Ji Ni.
- You're moving to that studio alone!

11
00:00:24,724 --> 00:00:26,693
- And you?
- I'm going to my art studio.

12
00:00:27,394 --> 00:00:30,330
That's a commercial building.
How would you even live there?

13
00:00:32,365 --> 00:00:33,600
I'm so sorry.

14
00:00:33,967 --> 00:00:36,803
I never imagined
something like this could happen.

15
00:00:36,903 --> 00:00:38,488
Of course you didn't.

16
00:00:38,571 --> 00:00:42,308
Dreaming only of what you wanted,
making plans all by yourself...

17
00:00:42,642 --> 00:00:44,811
What? Leave?

18
00:00:45,111 --> 00:00:47,380
Let me live on my own?

19
00:00:48,114 --> 00:00:50,517
Is that something a mother says?
Does that even make sense?

20
00:00:50,750 --> 00:00:53,253
- You and the Seo Chon family...
- Don't make excuses!

21
00:00:53,820 --> 00:00:56,689
Mom, you took out that loan long ago
and bet every last cent.

22
00:00:59,325 --> 00:01:02,762
You're beyond hopeless.

23
00:01:03,730 --> 00:01:06,366
I'm too stunned to even speak.

24
00:01:06,766 --> 00:01:08,601
Do you know what this home means?

25
00:01:08,968 --> 00:01:12,705
This home holds memories
of you, me, and my dad.

26
00:01:13,139 --> 00:01:15,241
And now you're making us leave?

27
00:01:16,543 --> 00:01:17,877
I'm sorry.

28
00:01:22,415 --> 00:01:24,284
Honestly...

29
00:02:12,599 --> 00:02:16,736
I'm giving it now, so it won't feel
like a trade when I get the clothes.

30
00:02:27,347 --> 00:02:29,015
- Mom!
- Yes?

31
00:02:29,716 --> 00:02:31,317
You heard about that other family?

32
00:02:31,451 --> 00:02:33,036
Yes. What happened?

33
00:02:33,119 --> 00:02:34,687
I hear Seung Woo went to help.

34
00:02:34,787 --> 00:02:36,489
I doubt he can do much.

35
00:02:36,823 --> 00:02:39,726
She handed everything over to that lawyer
without a second thought.

36
00:02:39,993 --> 00:02:40,944
My word!

37
00:02:41,027 --> 00:02:42,795
She knew nothing
about running a business...

38
00:02:42,896 --> 00:02:44,464
She got too greedy.

39
00:02:45,098 --> 00:02:47,934
Mai can't stop worrying about Ji Ni.

40
00:02:54,274 --> 00:02:55,475
Yes, what is it?

41
00:02:57,243 --> 00:02:58,778
How would I know just by looking?

42
00:03:01,548 --> 00:03:02,916
All right.

43
00:03:04,017 --> 00:03:06,136
Seung Woo met a senior colleague
to talk it over,

44
00:03:06,219 --> 00:03:08,154
and he's heading back to the office.

45
00:03:08,388 --> 00:03:09,773
He asked me to bring him something.

46
00:03:09,856 --> 00:03:10,957
Says he'll be up all night.

47
00:03:11,124 --> 00:03:12,859
- All right, go ahead.
- Yes.

48
00:03:28,074 --> 00:03:30,043
Seung Hyun went out.

49
00:03:31,077 --> 00:03:33,246
I know.

50
00:03:35,582 --> 00:03:37,584
I'm worried about Ji Ni's family.

51
00:03:37,951 --> 00:03:40,520
I hope they didn't lose
a lifetime of savings.

52
00:03:43,489 --> 00:03:46,326
Why look at me like that? It frightens me.

53
00:03:47,560 --> 00:03:51,464
My mom says the mistress
is getting what she deserves.

54
00:03:51,898 --> 00:03:53,766
And poor Ji Ni is paying for it too.

55
00:03:54,000 --> 00:03:55,685
How can you say such a thing?

56
00:03:55,768 --> 00:03:59,556
They say whoever makes others cry
ends up shedding tears of blood.

57
00:03:59,639 --> 00:04:01,474
Quiet! Someone might hear you!

58
00:04:01,741 --> 00:04:04,143
You don't say things like that
about someone else's misfortune.

59
00:04:04,244 --> 00:04:07,280
I held it back for Ji Ni's sake...

60
00:04:07,447 --> 00:04:09,949
But I think my mom is right.

61
00:05:09,075 --> 00:05:13,379
Dad... What do we do now?

62
00:05:16,015 --> 00:05:18,217
We lost the house too.

63
00:05:19,352 --> 00:05:22,355
What are we going to do?

64
00:05:27,527 --> 00:05:30,630
Dad...

65
00:05:30,997 --> 00:05:34,133
How can there be no parking spots
this late at night?

66
00:05:34,934 --> 00:05:36,536
- What is it?
- She is crying.

67
00:05:37,270 --> 00:05:38,338
Ji Ni?

68
00:05:44,177 --> 00:05:45,244
Dad...

69
00:05:58,057 --> 00:05:59,125
Dad...

70
00:06:05,264 --> 00:06:06,316
(Cosmetics, Misc.)

71
00:06:06,399 --> 00:06:07,567
(Socks, Underwear, Ornaments)

72
00:06:33,960 --> 00:06:35,762
You're here?

73
00:06:38,030 --> 00:06:42,902
No matter how much I tidy this place,
why does it never look tidy?

74
00:06:44,170 --> 00:06:45,538
Have some breakfast.

75
00:06:45,705 --> 00:06:47,073
I'll wash up and head to work.

76
00:06:48,908 --> 00:06:50,042
Wait...

77
00:06:51,110 --> 00:06:53,479
Sleeping at the studio must be hard,

78
00:06:53,846 --> 00:06:56,215
I'll put a cot in here, so come sleep.

79
00:06:57,683 --> 00:06:59,085
It's the same either way.

80
00:07:01,587 --> 00:07:03,322
I have nothing to say.

81
00:07:03,623 --> 00:07:04,891
I'm sorry, sweetheart.

82
00:07:13,166 --> 00:07:14,434
You've been drinking again?

83
00:07:15,735 --> 00:07:17,854
That was the first time, yesterday.

84
00:07:17,937 --> 00:07:20,406
You make me sound like an alcoholic.

85
00:07:22,074 --> 00:07:23,760
You said you'd stop drinking.

86
00:07:23,843 --> 00:07:26,479
You promised to leave the wine behind,
but you insisted on bringing it.

87
00:07:26,612 --> 00:07:28,264
Should I throw out what I paid for?

88
00:07:28,347 --> 00:07:30,216
You threw away far more than that.

89
00:07:30,516 --> 00:07:32,669
I'd toss this wine out of sheer disgust.

90
00:07:32,752 --> 00:07:35,888
If I don't have this, how am I supposed
to get through this without it?

91
00:07:36,255 --> 00:07:39,292
You know how long I hesitated
before opening this?

92
00:07:39,492 --> 00:07:42,428
"My Ji Ni will understand.
She knows how hard things are for me."

93
00:07:42,728 --> 00:07:44,130
That's what I told myself.

94
00:07:44,997 --> 00:07:46,132
You brat.

95
00:07:52,104 --> 00:07:53,906
The smell!

96
00:07:54,474 --> 00:07:56,008
This is unbearable!

97
00:07:56,676 --> 00:07:59,312
You brought this on yourself,
so don't complain!

98
00:08:28,641 --> 00:08:32,245
How long does he have
to eat plain porridge?

99
00:08:36,883 --> 00:08:39,051
O Reum!

100
00:08:39,385 --> 00:08:41,571
Just hold on a little longer.

101
00:08:41,654 --> 00:08:43,523
No!

102
00:08:43,656 --> 00:08:44,841
Poor thing.

103
00:08:44,924 --> 00:08:47,627
O Reum, just a little more!

104
00:08:47,793 --> 00:08:49,562
He must be sick of it.

105
00:08:49,896 --> 00:08:51,514
There's no other way.

106
00:08:51,597 --> 00:08:55,001
He has to bear it until the doctor
says, "That's enough."

107
00:08:56,903 --> 00:08:59,639
Do you know how that family is doing?

108
00:09:00,640 --> 00:09:04,143
No. All I heard is they moved
into a studio apartment.

109
00:09:04,377 --> 00:09:06,112
- And the company?
- They'll have to file for closure.

110
00:09:06,546 --> 00:09:09,482
Run a business like that
and even Bill Gates would go under.

111
00:09:09,882 --> 00:09:11,817
It's the price of greed.

112
00:09:11,918 --> 00:09:12,936
Exactly!

113
00:09:13,019 --> 00:09:14,921
It's punishment for being the other woman.

114
00:09:16,856 --> 00:09:18,641
What? Am I wrong?

115
00:09:18,724 --> 00:09:20,593
You can say that with O Reum right there?

116
00:09:20,927 --> 00:09:23,596
People turn cold awfully fast.

117
00:09:23,696 --> 00:09:25,665
I never said a word against Ji Ni.

118
00:09:25,965 --> 00:09:27,767
If anything, my heart aches for her.

119
00:09:27,967 --> 00:09:30,136
She's suffering for her mother's sake.

120
00:09:32,505 --> 00:09:35,107
Is there nothing we can do to help?

121
00:09:36,309 --> 00:09:38,945
They had us sign over our shares.

122
00:09:39,312 --> 00:09:40,746
There's nothing left to give.

123
00:09:41,080 --> 00:09:42,214
Just forget about it!

124
00:09:42,481 --> 00:09:44,984
Everyone has to fend for themselves now.

125
00:09:45,484 --> 00:09:46,752
By the way, Mother,

126
00:09:47,186 --> 00:09:49,789
What's this hairpin? It looks expensive.

127
00:09:50,723 --> 00:09:52,525
This? It's nothing, really...

128
00:09:53,259 --> 00:09:54,978
A student gave it to me.

129
00:09:55,061 --> 00:09:59,098
Mom, why don't you ever wear the hairpin
I bought with my first paycheck?

130
00:09:59,632 --> 00:10:00,917
I do wear it!

131
00:10:01,000 --> 00:10:03,135
You bought me one little thing
and act like it's such a big deal...

132
00:10:04,937 --> 00:10:06,072
Just go find a job!

133
00:10:07,306 --> 00:10:09,442
- Find a job.
- Find a job.

134
00:10:12,445 --> 00:10:14,280
O Reum, isn't it good?

135
00:10:14,580 --> 00:10:16,415
Eat plenty.

136
00:10:17,516 --> 00:10:19,251
No word from the police?

137
00:10:19,986 --> 00:10:21,153
None.

138
00:10:21,287 --> 00:10:23,522
Where did you move to?

139
00:10:23,956 --> 00:10:25,424
I just moved somewhere for now.

140
00:10:26,092 --> 00:10:28,260
There's nothing more I can do for you,

141
00:10:28,427 --> 00:10:30,763
so file for closure and wind it down.

142
00:10:30,896 --> 00:10:33,099
All right. I'll get to it.

143
00:10:34,066 --> 00:10:35,434
You don't want to close it?

144
00:10:36,035 --> 00:10:39,489
You said it makes no difference
either way, so why keep pushing me?

145
00:10:39,572 --> 00:10:41,207
This was my husband's business.

146
00:10:41,340 --> 00:10:43,242
Do you think I want to shut it down?

147
00:10:43,509 --> 00:10:46,512
Doesn't it feel strange,
talking to me about my father?

148
00:10:47,480 --> 00:10:50,500
This happened because you were too naive.

149
00:10:50,583 --> 00:10:51,684
Excuse me?

150
00:10:52,251 --> 00:10:56,389
You take what isn't yours if you like it,
and stake the house because it pays...

151
00:10:56,756 --> 00:10:58,908
How can a person have no boundaries?

152
00:10:58,991 --> 00:11:00,426
Boundaries?

153
00:11:00,726 --> 00:11:02,628
What did I ever take?

154
00:11:03,029 --> 00:11:06,032
Your mother again? Fine.

155
00:11:06,198 --> 00:11:08,234
I wondered when that would come up.

156
00:11:08,334 --> 00:11:10,202
Now that I'm down, I'm an easy target?

157
00:11:10,403 --> 00:11:14,874
When you needed the marrow, you two came
ready to give me the shirt off your back.

158
00:11:15,041 --> 00:11:16,960
Was that last month or last year?

159
00:11:17,043 --> 00:11:19,378
That's why I came to help, at least.

160
00:11:19,478 --> 00:11:21,313
Right. Thank you.

161
00:11:21,447 --> 00:11:23,683
Sure. Don't call me again.

162
00:11:25,785 --> 00:11:27,453
Hey! Cha Seung Woo!

163
00:11:28,454 --> 00:11:29,555
What?

164
00:11:29,822 --> 00:11:31,257
You drove here, didn't you?

165
00:11:31,390 --> 00:11:33,192
Drop me at the terminal on your way.

166
00:11:33,325 --> 00:11:34,660
Why would I?

167
00:11:36,529 --> 00:11:38,698
You're unemployed anyway.
Can't you spare me some pity?

168
00:11:39,165 --> 00:11:41,767
I'm a widow who lost everything.

169
00:11:42,234 --> 00:11:44,670
I have a guest performance out of town.

170
00:11:44,770 --> 00:11:46,205
To earn every penny I can.

171
00:11:52,645 --> 00:11:55,848
O Reum, thanks to you,
I'm learning real patience.

172
00:11:58,818 --> 00:12:01,471
Yes. Still no word from the police.

173
00:12:01,554 --> 00:12:04,623
I'm on my way to a performance
out of town.

174
00:12:06,058 --> 00:12:09,295
I know. Only the music still welcomes me.

175
00:12:09,895 --> 00:12:11,397
Yes.

176
00:12:14,033 --> 00:12:17,903
If you give out too, I'll starve.

177
00:12:18,504 --> 00:12:22,441
- Isn't there a rich man out there?
- Sorry?

178
00:12:23,209 --> 00:12:26,863
Maybe I'll remarry
someone worth showing off,

179
00:12:26,946 --> 00:12:29,599
and play the devoted widow
who saves my late husband's company.

180
00:12:29,682 --> 00:12:32,184
Stop sacrificing other people's lives.

181
00:12:32,384 --> 00:12:34,386
I'm telling you this as a human being.

182
00:12:35,521 --> 00:12:38,524
Advice from a man who's been through it.
I'll take it to heart.

183
00:12:43,162 --> 00:12:46,332
Open the door.

184
00:12:48,434 --> 00:12:50,069
Find your own way.

185
00:12:50,336 --> 00:12:53,439
Why so petty? It was a joke.

186
00:12:53,572 --> 00:12:56,142
Do you not know the difference
between what to say and what not to?

187
00:12:56,342 --> 00:12:58,077
I'm not your son.

188
00:12:58,244 --> 00:13:01,180
I try to hold back for O Reum's sake,
but I can't anymore.

189
00:13:01,614 --> 00:13:04,150
I'm sorry.

190
00:13:04,250 --> 00:13:06,786
I've just been all twisted up lately.

191
00:13:06,952 --> 00:13:10,790
After today, who knows when we'll meet.
Bear with me just once more.

192
00:13:11,624 --> 00:13:13,259
I'm sorry.

193
00:13:42,955 --> 00:13:44,056
Thank you.

194
00:13:54,400 --> 00:13:57,903
That far? All right.

195
00:13:58,637 --> 00:14:01,473
Travel safe. Yes.

196
00:14:03,108 --> 00:14:06,512
- Your mother?
- Yes. She's off to perform.

197
00:14:07,813 --> 00:14:10,482
Your mother's will to live is unreal.

198
00:14:11,517 --> 00:14:13,619
She's become a musician for survival.

199
00:14:13,719 --> 00:14:15,421
Not the kind of artist you mean.

200
00:14:15,588 --> 00:14:19,558
I thought she'd be flat on her back
for a month, or even two.

201
00:14:19,925 --> 00:14:21,827
If it were my mom, it'd be chaos.

202
00:14:22,027 --> 00:14:25,464
My mom would be the same
if my dad were still here.

203
00:14:25,631 --> 00:14:28,000
Now there's no one to lean on.

204
00:14:29,268 --> 00:14:31,320
- What are these drawings?
- The kids'.

205
00:14:31,403 --> 00:14:35,040
I asked for folktales and got tigers,
nine-tailed foxes, goblins...

206
00:14:35,474 --> 00:14:36,742
You name it, it's here.

207
00:14:36,909 --> 00:14:39,745
There's even King Danjong.
Is he a folktale character?

208
00:14:40,913 --> 00:14:41,931
Little rascals.

209
00:14:42,014 --> 00:14:42,648
(King Danjong)

210
00:14:47,519 --> 00:14:51,340
Look at you.
Your eyes light up when you see art.

211
00:14:51,423 --> 00:14:52,909
When I look at a drawing...

212
00:14:52,992 --> 00:14:55,094
I can escape into another world.

213
00:14:57,296 --> 00:14:59,832
Is that what genius is?
I wish I could do that.

214
00:15:01,834 --> 00:15:03,235
Don't tease me!

215
00:15:20,219 --> 00:15:21,487
It's chaos, isn't it?

216
00:15:22,054 --> 00:15:24,790
It is. Her focus is remarkable.

217
00:15:27,760 --> 00:15:29,995
It's a bit much.

218
00:15:31,063 --> 00:15:32,231
Why that look on your face?

219
00:15:32,331 --> 00:15:34,300
You admire a genius from a distance.

220
00:15:34,466 --> 00:15:36,568
Up close, they're just annoying.

221
00:15:41,507 --> 00:15:43,275
Hello there.

222
00:15:43,742 --> 00:15:45,444
- May I sit?
- Please.

223
00:15:48,714 --> 00:15:50,382
I was curious what you were drawing.

224
00:15:52,885 --> 00:15:56,021
The children drew these.
They gave me an idea...

225
00:15:56,488 --> 00:15:58,007
My father told me.

226
00:15:58,090 --> 00:16:00,426
That the folktale series
is turning out great.

227
00:16:01,360 --> 00:16:03,629
I wouldn't go that far.

228
00:16:04,129 --> 00:16:08,067
This one is a goblin. Isn't he cute?

229
00:16:08,767 --> 00:16:11,770
Did you know goblins
have terrible memories?

230
00:16:12,604 --> 00:16:15,774
He kept paying Mr. Kim every day
until he went broke.

231
00:16:16,275 --> 00:16:17,609
Fun, isn't it?

232
00:16:17,710 --> 00:16:20,579
And I love that goblin fire is blue.

233
00:16:21,613 --> 00:16:25,184
You could build a goblin series
around traits like that.

234
00:16:26,585 --> 00:16:28,687
Spoken like a director!

235
00:16:28,854 --> 00:16:30,189
Did I sound too much like a salesman?

236
00:16:31,490 --> 00:16:35,861
"Salesman" isn't quite right.
More like management?

237
00:16:36,061 --> 00:16:38,664
- I heard you majored in arts management.
- Yes.

238
00:16:40,199 --> 00:16:43,469
I heard things have been hard,
but drawing seems to make you happy.

239
00:16:46,038 --> 00:16:48,440
Drawing is my lifeline.

240
00:16:48,574 --> 00:16:51,460
No matter how hard things get,
once I sink into a drawing,

241
00:16:51,543 --> 00:16:53,545
I can forget the pain.

242
00:16:54,246 --> 00:16:56,565
Rather than simply capturing a moment,

243
00:16:56,648 --> 00:16:58,484
I prefer drawings that tell a story.

244
00:16:58,617 --> 00:17:00,119
That's why I work at the publisher.

245
00:17:00,252 --> 00:17:01,687
You really are an artist.

246
00:17:02,321 --> 00:17:04,690
Do you realize you're talking
more than ever?

247
00:17:04,857 --> 00:17:06,442
Thanks to the children's drawings?

248
00:17:06,525 --> 00:17:08,293
Maybe so?

249
00:17:14,099 --> 00:17:15,300
Ji Hu.

250
00:17:15,834 --> 00:17:17,369
You're here.

251
00:17:18,670 --> 00:17:20,539
What are you two doing side by side?

252
00:17:20,873 --> 00:17:22,274
I was looking at Ji Ni's drawings.

253
00:17:22,408 --> 00:17:23,609
Let's go.

254
00:17:23,709 --> 00:17:25,661
Let's talk about the goblin series
again sometime.

255
00:17:25,744 --> 00:17:26,862
Sure.

256
00:17:26,945 --> 00:17:28,280
Goblin what?

257
00:17:29,048 --> 00:17:30,766
I heard you're illustrating
children's books now?

258
00:17:30,849 --> 00:17:32,418
It's none of your business.

259
00:17:33,085 --> 00:17:35,954
How can you talk like that?

260
00:17:36,388 --> 00:17:38,457
You're hurting me.

261
00:17:41,427 --> 00:17:42,895
Let's go!

262
00:17:49,768 --> 00:17:51,503
You saw how Ji Ni talks, didn't you?

263
00:17:52,271 --> 00:17:54,907
She's always like that. So irritating.

264
00:17:55,340 --> 00:17:57,476
I'll get the car. Wait here.

265
00:17:58,410 --> 00:18:00,779
Why don't you say anything? I'm angry.

266
00:18:01,180 --> 00:18:02,598
That's between you and Ji Ni.

267
00:18:02,681 --> 00:18:03,766
Whose side should I take?

268
00:18:03,849 --> 00:18:06,885
Mine. Obviously, you take my side.

269
00:18:07,319 --> 00:18:08,571
Don't even speak to her.

270
00:18:08,654 --> 00:18:09,755
It upsets me.

271
00:18:10,389 --> 00:18:13,225
All right. What would cheer you up?

272
00:18:13,492 --> 00:18:16,895
Shopping. Chanel has new arrivals.

273
00:18:17,329 --> 00:18:19,431
Let's go look so I can post photos.

274
00:18:19,731 --> 00:18:21,700
So shopping is your lifeline.

275
00:18:22,468 --> 00:18:24,436
That's right. It keeps me alive.

276
00:18:27,406 --> 00:18:29,341
Don't look at me like that!

277
00:18:29,775 --> 00:18:33,045
I was up all night again,
coming up with ideas for my work.

278
00:18:33,345 --> 00:18:34,913
I see.

279
00:18:35,280 --> 00:18:37,049
- Wait right here.
- Okay.

280
00:18:47,426 --> 00:18:48,727
Na Ji Ni.

281
00:18:49,361 --> 00:18:52,498
I've put up with you for far too long
for Ji Hu's sake.

282
00:18:52,898 --> 00:18:55,701
How dare someone like you talk to Ji Hu?

283
00:18:57,736 --> 00:18:59,304
Damn it...

284
00:18:59,738 --> 00:19:02,040
Time to put out some roach poison.

285
00:19:09,681 --> 00:19:11,049
Sa Bin.

286
00:19:11,450 --> 00:19:13,152
Sun Kyung.

287
00:19:13,919 --> 00:19:16,138
What brings you here?
Weren't you at the reunion?

288
00:19:16,221 --> 00:19:18,223
I was. I did go, but...

289
00:19:18,724 --> 00:19:21,210
My stomach was upset after lunch,
so I left early.

290
00:19:21,293 --> 00:19:24,313
On my way home, I thought
I'd stop for acupuncture.

291
00:19:24,396 --> 00:19:26,115
You did well to come. Please go in.

292
00:19:26,198 --> 00:19:27,399
All right.

293
00:19:28,167 --> 00:19:30,319
The weather's gloomy today,

294
00:19:30,402 --> 00:19:32,688
so you must have been off, Sun Kyung.

295
00:19:32,771 --> 00:19:34,239
Let me give you a warm compress.

296
00:19:34,406 --> 00:19:35,424
Thank you.

297
00:19:35,507 --> 00:19:38,143
I heard about No Yeong Ju.

298
00:19:38,277 --> 00:19:39,811
Did you?

299
00:19:40,179 --> 00:19:43,148
She was the best singer in our class,

300
00:19:43,448 --> 00:19:45,050
and everyone remembered her.

301
00:19:45,417 --> 00:19:48,137
She studied voice, then musical theater.

302
00:19:48,220 --> 00:19:50,122
Musical theater. I see.

303
00:19:50,222 --> 00:19:52,057
She never got to debut.

304
00:19:52,257 --> 00:19:53,825
She married young,

305
00:19:54,293 --> 00:19:56,528
and her husband had an affair.

306
00:19:56,662 --> 00:19:58,964
He kept two households,

307
00:19:59,064 --> 00:20:01,800
so she spent most of her life
living like a widow,

308
00:20:02,367 --> 00:20:04,369
I didn't hear the rest.

309
00:20:04,736 --> 00:20:07,256
They said everyone lost touch
after graduation.

310
00:20:07,339 --> 00:20:10,142
- Her husband probably died young.
- Not true.

311
00:20:10,442 --> 00:20:13,512
I heard he had an affair
with some woman who played violin.

312
00:20:13,879 --> 00:20:17,082
Anyway, I'm not really interested
in this sort of talk,

313
00:20:17,416 --> 00:20:20,035
but since you'd mentioned her before,
I listened.

314
00:20:20,118 --> 00:20:21,320
Enough.

315
00:20:21,687 --> 00:20:23,072
Don't dwell on it.

316
00:20:23,155 --> 00:20:26,558
You're so clean-minded,
that's why such talk bothers you.

317
00:20:27,259 --> 00:20:28,377
That's right.

318
00:20:28,460 --> 00:20:31,263
I truly can't stand people
who lose their temper,

319
00:20:31,363 --> 00:20:34,066
or spread gossip about others.

320
00:20:34,666 --> 00:20:36,168
Please rest for a while.

321
00:20:38,704 --> 00:20:40,872
My stomach feels a bit better.

322
00:20:51,149 --> 00:20:53,719
You don't know this song?
It's an Italian art song.

323
00:20:54,319 --> 00:20:55,520
You majored in voice, didn't you?

324
00:20:59,091 --> 00:21:02,394
I know it. It just caught me off guard.

325
00:21:05,564 --> 00:21:07,466
So you missed the reunion after all?

326
00:21:07,766 --> 00:21:08,851
What's the point of going?

327
00:21:08,934 --> 00:21:11,770
It's all bragging
about their husbands and children.

328
00:21:12,170 --> 00:21:14,706
You could brag about your beauty.

329
00:21:14,973 --> 00:21:15,807
Sorry?

330
00:21:16,875 --> 00:21:19,411
Thank you. You're the only one, Sa Bin.

331
00:21:19,978 --> 00:21:22,698
Sun Kyung came back from there
with an upset stomach,

332
00:21:22,781 --> 00:21:24,082
so I gave her acupuncture.

333
00:21:24,316 --> 00:21:26,852
- That's when I heard.
- I see.

334
00:21:33,625 --> 00:21:34,777
What is it?

335
00:21:34,860 --> 00:21:36,628
Do you want to try that?

336
00:21:42,167 --> 00:21:43,835
Having a girlfriend beside me,

337
00:21:44,703 --> 00:21:47,539
winning her a doll from a claw machine
is something I've always wanted to do.

338
00:21:47,906 --> 00:21:49,374
A girlfriend...

339
00:21:49,474 --> 00:21:50,526
Go ahead and try.

340
00:21:50,609 --> 00:21:52,844
They say these are rigged, though.

341
00:21:53,712 --> 00:21:56,748
These hands are made for acupuncture.
They're delicate, so I'm good at this.

342
00:22:09,094 --> 00:22:10,896
Come on.

343
00:22:14,032 --> 00:22:16,518
- Let me...
- Sa Bin, that's enough.

344
00:22:16,601 --> 00:22:18,704
You're just scratching its back.

345
00:22:20,105 --> 00:22:21,490
You can make that face too?

346
00:22:21,573 --> 00:22:25,494
Watch. This time I'll get it for sure
and give it to you.

347
00:22:25,577 --> 00:22:27,412
Come on, now.

348
00:22:28,280 --> 00:22:29,481
I can do this...

349
00:22:38,957 --> 00:22:41,410
Yeong Ju, do you want a turn?

350
00:22:41,493 --> 00:22:43,912
This is genuinely hard.

351
00:22:43,995 --> 00:22:47,332
Weren't those delicate acupuncture hands?

352
00:22:48,100 --> 00:22:50,202
All right, let me try.

353
00:22:54,272 --> 00:22:57,275
Yes, that's it. Just a bit more!

354
00:23:10,055 --> 00:23:11,456
That was easy.

355
00:23:12,524 --> 00:23:16,928
You know I moved it
into an easy spot for you, right?

356
00:23:17,062 --> 00:23:19,531
How petty of you to say that.

357
00:23:21,466 --> 00:23:23,301
Here. A gift.

358
00:23:23,535 --> 00:23:24,653
- What?
- I mean...

359
00:23:24,736 --> 00:23:27,289
You said you moved it into an easy spot.

360
00:23:27,372 --> 00:23:29,207
So it belongs to you.

361
00:23:29,508 --> 00:23:31,126
You're really giving it to me?

362
00:23:31,209 --> 00:23:32,411
Yes.

363
00:23:39,885 --> 00:23:41,203
I think one more try will do it.

364
00:23:41,286 --> 00:23:42,687
Hold on, just one more.

365
00:23:43,054 --> 00:23:45,007
- Stop!
- Please, I know I can get it.

366
00:23:45,090 --> 00:23:46,491
One more time!

367
00:23:58,537 --> 00:24:00,539
You startled me...

368
00:24:00,906 --> 00:24:03,141
I knocked. You just didn't hear it.

369
00:24:03,375 --> 00:24:05,510
Right. What is it?

370
00:24:05,710 --> 00:24:08,680
So, there's this person,

371
00:24:09,147 --> 00:24:10,933
Not a woman.

372
00:24:11,016 --> 00:24:13,819
And whatever this person says...

373
00:24:14,486 --> 00:24:16,688
if it all sounds like encouragement...

374
00:24:17,122 --> 00:24:18,523
that means we're close, right?

375
00:24:18,723 --> 00:24:20,425
It's a woman, isn't it?

376
00:24:20,525 --> 00:24:23,128
I told you, it isn't a woman.

377
00:24:24,229 --> 00:24:27,466
Every word from this person
sounds like encouragement?

378
00:24:28,099 --> 00:24:29,685
You need acupuncture. You're not fine.

379
00:24:29,768 --> 00:24:32,404
Im Ji Hu, it's your mouth
that needs the needle.

380
00:24:32,671 --> 00:24:35,140
Even parents and kids
don't just cheer each other on.

381
00:24:35,240 --> 00:24:38,343
Sa Bin, that's either an illness or love.

382
00:24:41,279 --> 00:24:43,298
- Am I wrong?
- Yes, you're wrong.

383
00:24:43,381 --> 00:24:45,717
You're being strange.

384
00:24:46,918 --> 00:24:48,987
Why did I even ask?

385
00:24:52,491 --> 00:24:53,692
Who could it be?

386
00:24:54,292 --> 00:24:56,328
It can't be that grandmother.

387
00:24:57,496 --> 00:24:59,431
Who on earth is he hiding?

388
00:25:03,869 --> 00:25:06,671
- Ji Ni.
- You should've stayed over.

389
00:25:07,672 --> 00:25:10,008
Staying over costs money.

390
00:25:11,076 --> 00:25:13,144
They told me to stay...

391
00:25:13,712 --> 00:25:15,580
Still, home is more comfortable.

392
00:25:15,747 --> 00:25:17,516
If you can call this a home.

393
00:25:20,185 --> 00:25:23,872
They said I would strike it rich
in middle age.

394
00:25:23,955 --> 00:25:25,257
It was all a lie.

395
00:25:25,957 --> 00:25:28,093
Here, drink up.

396
00:25:33,698 --> 00:25:35,500
That hits the spot.

397
00:25:37,769 --> 00:25:40,605
- What about you?
- No reason.

398
00:25:42,507 --> 00:25:44,142
It's hard, isn't it?

399
00:25:47,579 --> 00:25:51,883
I dug this hole myself,
but I'm sorry you're paying for it.

400
00:25:53,418 --> 00:25:56,888
- I'll bring warm water.
- No, I'll do it in the bathroom.

401
00:25:57,622 --> 00:26:00,525
- You said the bathroom smells.
- Ji Ni, really...

402
00:26:07,599 --> 00:26:09,734
She takes after you.

403
00:26:18,476 --> 00:26:19,678
Here you are!

404
00:26:21,546 --> 00:26:24,082
All right, here we go...

405
00:26:27,319 --> 00:26:28,887
This feels wonderful.

406
00:26:30,488 --> 00:26:33,358
Thank you, sweetheart.

407
00:26:34,559 --> 00:26:35,760
Get some rest.

408
00:26:36,528 --> 00:26:37,729
You're leaving?

409
00:26:38,096 --> 00:26:41,166
I'm worried about you staying
in that commercial building. Sleep here.

410
00:26:41,666 --> 00:26:42,867
I'm more comfortable there.

411
00:26:42,968 --> 00:26:44,636
That's my home now too.

412
00:26:49,641 --> 00:26:50,842
I'm off.

413
00:26:52,344 --> 00:26:56,147
Text me when you get there.

414
00:27:13,965 --> 00:27:15,600
You fool.

415
00:27:17,702 --> 00:27:19,204
Na Se Ri.

416
00:27:19,804 --> 00:27:21,473
Pull yourself together.

417
00:27:26,244 --> 00:27:28,179
You're not even worth crying over.

418
00:27:58,543 --> 00:28:01,797
(Family Register)

419
00:28:01,880 --> 00:28:03,848
I'm thinking
of teaching private lessons again.

420
00:28:03,982 --> 00:28:05,100
You know how good I am.

421
00:28:05,183 --> 00:28:06,335
Your hands are shaking.

422
00:28:06,418 --> 00:28:07,536
Your pulse is very weak.

423
00:28:07,619 --> 00:28:09,338
What's happening? Why is this?

424
00:28:09,421 --> 00:28:12,774
The rumors are true. Anyone
who breaks up a family shouldn't prosper.

425
00:28:12,857 --> 00:28:14,376
Punishment or reward,

426
00:28:14,459 --> 00:28:15,911
who are you to decide?

427
00:28:15,994 --> 00:28:18,113
You said we should live together.
That's the plan.

428
00:28:18,196 --> 00:28:19,881
I knew you weren't in your right mind,

429
00:28:19,964 --> 00:28:21,316
but please respect some boundaries.

430
00:28:21,399 --> 00:28:23,952
You said you'd do anything
to keep O Reum alive.

431
00:28:24,035 --> 00:28:25,236
Se Ri!

432
00:28:27,305 --> 00:28:29,507
(Subtitles are provided by KOCOWA.)
